 ## Unreleased
 
+- Fix: host-uid shadow bindings go with their rows. `MessageStore.delete_session_messages` and `/lcm doctor clean
+  apply` delete the `host_uid_bindings` of the deleted store ids in the same transaction, so a reused store id
+  never inherits a stale binding; a store without the table is left without it. The persisted lineage key is now
+  `<home_tag>:<root>` (`home_tag` = first 16 hex chars of the sha256 of the resolved `state.db` path), so Hermes
+  homes sharing one LCM database no longer mix bindings of same-id roots. Bindings recorded under the old
+  bare-root keys are no longer matched. (#836)
+
